{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB00768 - MONDO_grouped_11786_5324_24332",
  "verbalization": "Olopatadine is implicated in the pathogenesis of Allergic Rhinitis through its indication for Vasomotor Rhinitis, which is a condition characterized by nasal symptoms triggered by non-immunological factors. The evidence suggests that Olopatadine may exert a therapeutic effect on Allergic Rhinitis via a mechanism that involves the modulation of vasomotor responses, as it is indicated for conditions like Vasomotor Rhinitis and is linked to other agents such as Mebhydrolin and Mizolastine, which also target similar pathways. These agents are known to inhibit histamine receptors and modulate inflammatory responses, which are central to allergic reactions. The shared indication for Vasomotor Rhinitis across Olopatadine and its derivatives implies a common mechanism of action, potentially involving the suppression of inflammatory mediators or vascular overactivity. The integration of these pathways supports the hypothesis that Olopatadine may have a role in the treatment of Allergic Rhinitis through a mechanism that involves the modulation of vasomotor symptoms, though further mechanistic validation is required to confirm the direct relationship between Olopatadine and the disease.",
